cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use gamdid in your research, please cite it using the preferred citation below."
type: software
title: "gamdid: Inference and Visualization for Differential Distribution Analysis in Single Cell Proteomics"
abstract: >-
  gamdid provides inference and interpretable visualizations for comparing
  distributions in single cell proteomics data. It recasts density estimation
  as a Poisson regression and uses generalized additive models (GAMs) to
  flexibly model distributions and test for any distributional difference
  between groups. The GAM p-value is aggregated with the msqrob2 p-value via
  the harmonic mean p-value to improve power for mean shifts. gamdid also
  detects differential regions of the distribution and supports omnibus
  testing across more than two groups, with post-hoc pairwise comparisons via
  stagewise testing.
